# message-chain (#14, Fowler "Hide Delegate"): a member-access chain
# 'a.b.c.d...' in value-expression context deeper than the configurable
# threshold (default 4 dotted hops -- fires at 5+ hops). Hop-count definition:
# the number of dotted member accesses off the base identifier -- 'a.b.c.d.e'
# is 4 hops (b, c, d, e). Flagged once, at the outermost exprDot (start of the
# whole chain, i.e. the base identifier's position). ON by default.
# Line 10 'Order.Customer.Address.City.Zip.Length' -- 5 hops (Customer,
# Address, City, Zip, Length), 5 > 4 -> FLAGGED.
message-chain 10
# Line 11 'Order.Customer.Name' -- 2 hops (Customer, Name), 2 <= 4 -> not
# flagged (short chain, ordinary field/property access).
!message-chain 11
# Line 12 'Order.Customer.Address.Zip.Value.Digits.Count' -- 6 hops
# (Customer, Address, Zip, Value, Digits, Count), 6 > 4 -> FLAGGED.
message-chain 12
